WEBVTT


00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.266
we're gonna start with a Japanese Katsudon

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:11.943
mmm

00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:12.940
that's really good

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:14.321
mhhmmm

00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:16.371
“what a delightful treat”

00:00:23.421 --> 00:00:25.520
Japanese food doesn't really use a lot of seasoning

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:27.921
but somehow they just make it taste so good

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.347
honestly the only thing I would change

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:30.160
about this is just

00:00:30.161 --> 00:00:31.560
I'd make it a little bit more spicy

00:00:31.608 --> 00:00:32.612
cuz it’s not spicy at all

00:00:32.672 --> 00:00:34.224
next up we have a Korean Bulgogi

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:35.690
mhmmm

00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:36.900
“yummy”

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.427
hmm

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:42.426
this is great

00:00:42.427 --> 00:00:44.521
but again I just wish it was a little bit more spicy

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:45.960
both of these dishes were good

00:00:45.961 --> 00:00:47.357
but only one can win

00:00:47.415 --> 00:00:48.191
so which one was better?

00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:49.560
oh man this is tough

00:00:49.594 --> 00:00:50.723
so I guess it’s a tie

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:52.537
ohh

00:00:52.604 --> 00:00:54.580
the Japanese dish came with some Miso Soup
